Z||000000||maryjane||09-15-2001||08:48 PM||||I occasionally get email pictures in MIME format, in an attachment. Evidently, Earthlink doesn't display mime. Is there anyway to make it display these .jpg file that are sent in mime format. Failing this, anyone suggest a good free mail server that I could use as a second mail server? thanks.<BR>Don||||reg||1
Z||000001||Haagster||09-15-2001||09:07 PM||||Last I heard (a few years ago), Winzip will decompress MIME files so they can be displayed.  I don't know if the current version will do it or not, but I'll look into it.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature_4.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000002||Haagster||09-16-2001||07:21 AM||||This information came from the TechTV web site (formerly ZDTV)(www.techtv.com).  Hope this helps...<P><BR>Q: I have tried to email JPG formatted pictures to friends who are on AOL, but the pictures are being reformatted to MIME. Can my friends still view these pictures? If so, how do they return them to the original format? These are baby pictures and everyone wants to see them. Thanks.<P>---phone call from Jim in North Las Vegas, Nevada <P>A: We recommend that you upgrade to AOL 4.0. If this doesn't solve the problem, then you can try using WinZip to unMIME the file. Detach the file and drag it onto WinZip. You can get WinZip from the ZDNet Software Library. <P>If the file did not arrive as an attachment, look for some gobblydegook at the bottom of the message. Highlight it and paste it into a text file. Save it and then drag that it over WinZip. <P>In the old days, not all machines could transmit data over the Net at an eight-bits-per-byte ratio. MIME (Multi-Purpose Internet Mail Extension) was invented to convert files from eight-bit to six-bit, thus streamlining the files and making it more likely that your attachment would go through. <P>A text file will still display properly at six or seven bits. But if you're sending a video, graphics, audio, or programs, you will not be able to see the file at all. <P><p>[This message has been edited by Haagster (edited 09-16-2001).]||||reg||1
